TOON_FILE: STORY_CONTEXT.toon | VERSION: 1

## Story
GOAL: Overhaul news pipeline to reduce news-to-decision latency from ~10 min to <2 min, eliminate 19,800 regex scans/cycle, and give AI narrative-threaded context instead of isolated headlines
TYPE: Backend infrastructure improvement (4 phases)
SOURCE: NEWS_PIPELINE_PLAN.md (850-line detailed plan)

## Acceptance Criteria
- News-to-decision latency <2 min for Guardian-sourced breaking news
- News-to-decision latency <4 min for RSS-sourced news
- 0 regex scans at query time (was 19,800 per cycle)
- AI receives narrative-threaded news grouped by developing stories
- AI receives previous signal for maintain/flip reasoning
- Breaking news from any source triggers immediate ensemble re-run (debounced 1/min)
- Guardian API polls at 2-min interval (2,880 req/day, within 5,000/day free tier)
- RSS Tier-1 feeds poll at 3 min, India-specific at 5 min, Tier-2 at 10 min
- parseRssDate fallback events are logged
- Monday morning news gets priority over weekend noise (freshness bonus)
- GDELT fetches every 5 min (was 15 min)
- Asset pre-tagging at ingestion time eliminates query-time scanning
- No new API keys needed (all existing in .env)
- No external WebSocket dependency

## User Flow
  RSS feed publishes article
      → 1-3 min (RSS poll) or <2 min (Guardian API)
  processArticle() runs
      → URL dedup → semantic dedup → DB INSERT → asset pre-tagging
      → is_breaking keyword check
      → if breaking + market open → trigger ensemble re-run
  AI ensemble runs (per-asset, 3 windows: 6h/24h/72h)
      → Gets narrative-threaded news block (stories, not headlines)
      → Gets previous signal (maintain or flip)
      → Gets "what changed" context if breaking-triggered
  Hot context updated
      → Tick evaluator reads on next tick (<1 sec)

## Scope Boundaries
IN_SCOPE:
- Phase 1: Bug fixes (parseRssDate logging, article cap increase, freshness bonus, GDELT interval)
- Phase 2: Guardian API fast-poll + RSS interval reduction + is_breaking column
- Phase 3: DB INSERT trigger for breaking news → immediate AI re-evaluation
- Phase 4: Narrative threading + asset pre-tagging + previous signal injection

OUT_OF_SCOPE (from "What NOT to Change" section):
- RSS polling architecture (stays as base, just interval tweaks)
- Semantic dedup (stays, enhanced with narrative_sequence_id)
- Hot context architecture (stays — in-memory, lock-free, atomic swap)
- Tick evaluator (stays — reads hot context on next tick)
- Trading strategy / gating logic (unchanged)
- News Trunk WebSocket (removed — unverified, unreliable)
- GNews/NewsAPI.org in ingestion pipeline (too limited for free tier)

## Dependencies
- Guardian API key: GUARDIAN_KEY (already in .env)
- GPT-4o API (existing, used for ensemble + event extraction)
- PostgreSQL (existing, needs migrations for is_breaking, narrative_sequence_id, article_asset_tags)
- Existing RSS infrastructure (feed-registry-seed.ts, rss-fetcher.ts, scheduler.ts)
- Existing semantic dedup (semantic-dedup.ts)
- Existing market scheduler (market/scheduler.ts, market-agent.ts)

## Similar Features in Codebase
- RSS ingestion: artifacts/api-server/src/services/ingestion/scheduler.ts
- RSS fetching: artifacts/api-server/src/services/ingestion/rss-fetcher.ts
- Feed registry: artifacts/api-server/src/services/ingestion/feed-registry-seed.ts
- Semantic dedup: artifacts/api-server/src/services/ingestion/semantic-dedup.ts
- News-to-asset matching: artifacts/api-server/src/services/market/stock-news.ts
- Market scheduler: artifacts/api-server/src/services/market/scheduler.ts
- AI agent: artifacts/api-server/src/services/market/market-agent.ts
- News display route (uses Guardian/NewsAPI/GNews): artifacts/api-server/src/routes/news.ts
- DB schema: lib/db/src/schema/raw-articles.ts

## Design Direction
N/A — backend infrastructure only, no UI changes

## Constraints
- Free tier only: Guardian 5,000 req/day, GNews 100 req/day, NewsAPI 100 req/day + 1-day delay
- No external WebSocket dependency (News Trunk removed)
- RSS IP block risk: faster polling must be moderate, quarantine system as safety net
- GPT-4o API: 99 calls per 5-min cycle already, breaking news triggers must be debounced
- DB migrations must be backwards-compatible (additive, not destructive)
- processArticle latency: pre-tagging adds ~3ms, acceptable vs 2-5 sec embedding+dedup

## Implementation Phases
PHASE_1: Bug fixes (parseRssDate logging, article cap, freshness bonus, GDELT interval) — ~40 min
PHASE_2: Guardian API fast-poll + RSS interval reduction + is_breaking column — ~3 hours
PHASE_3: DB INSERT trigger → immediate AI re-evaluation — ~2.5 hours
PHASE_4: Narrative threading + asset pre-tagging + previous signal — ~7 hours
TOTAL: ~13 hours
